{
  "_id": "f90f9a4bb2fc2734",
  "name": "Wraith",
  "type": "character",
  "img": "systems/heroic5e/assets/characters/wraith/portrait.png",
  "system": {
    "biography": "<h2>Eddie Swazey</h2><p>A ghostly enhanced hero who phases between the living world and Limbo/Purgatory, slipping through walls, avoiding harm, and speaking with spirits of the dead.</p><h3>Backstory</h3><p>Eddie Swazey became Wraith after the Pulse changed his body into something partially out of phase with the physical world. His powers make him an infiltrator, protector, and uneasy bridge between the living and the dead.</p><h3>Costume</h3><p>Ghostly EMF signature; phase-sense altered physiology.</p>",
    "notes": "<p>Stealth and infiltration<br>Reading emotions and motives<br>Spotting danger and surveillance details<br>Driving and vehicle handling<br>Spirit communication and death-related occult clues</p><p>Level 1: Inner Fortress<br>Level 1: Force of Will</p><p>Cannot be surprised while conscious.<br>Advantage on saves against Shaken, Frightened, Dazed, and Charmed.<br>Once per encounter, reroll a failed save.<br>When using Steady On or Second Wind, gain temporary HP equal to WIS.<br>Can maintain phased state without it ending when attacking or using powers; attacks and powers work normally while selectively solid at the point of contact.</p><p>Solid Ground Required.<br>Phasing passes through the living world but not through beings, objects, obstacles, or barriers in Limbo/Purgatory. Physical attacks and damage from phased beings or Limbo/Purgatory sources affect Wraith normally while phased.</p>",
    "side": "Heroic",
    "calling": "Boy Scout",
    "triggers": {
      "minor": "Use phasing to protect or rescue someone who cannot protect themselves.",
      "major": "Enter danger alone by phasing through a barrier, wall, or hostile space so allies or civilians can escape.",
      "defining": "Suffer a major loss, defeat, or injury because you refused to abandon innocent people or trapped spirits."
    },
