    {
      "_id": "2e88dedebab4fb6c",
      "name": "Phasing",
      "type": "power",
      "img": "icons/svg/explosion.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>PHASING 1 - Power Effect Value: 15<br>Passive Benefits: Selectively phase individual limbs, whole body, or objects in contact with you. Fully phased, physical attacks cannot target you; you cannot interact with physical objects and pass through solid matter at normal speed.<br>Phase Through (Tier 1 At-Will, Bonus Action): Move up to Close range (25 ft) through solid matter without provoking Reactions. Must end in open space.<br>Disruptive Phase (Tier 1 Encounter, Action): Close range. Attack 1d20 + CON + Rank Bonus vs Parry/Block. Hit: 2d8 + CON physical damage bypassing armor and worn equipment. Target rolls 1d20 + CON vs EV 15. Failure: Dazed until end of next turn. Success: Shaken until end of next turn.<br>Walk Through Walls 1 (Utility): Outside combat, phase through solid barriers of any thickness at normal speed while carrying worn/held items.<br>Phase Slip 1 (Utility): Free action once per Turn, extend phased state to one object carried or worn.</p>",
        "subtype": "Power Set",
        "action": "Passive",
        "category": "Power Set",
        "source": "Heroic 5e v2.4",
        "prerequisite": "",
        "tier": "",
        "powerSet": "Phasing",
